00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Now we have a model with movements and a well-dressed costume.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
In order to make a more stable animation, we need to make some adjustments to the costume.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Like a belt-like version that is smaller and easier to slide.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
In addition to reducing the particle diameter, it can also be used to increase the friction coefficient to prevent sliding.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Using a sewing tool can fix a certain point of the costume on another point.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
This function is similar to the fixed to the virtual model.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Using a sewing tool can find the fixed to the virtual model tool.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Using this tool can put the costume on the virtual model, and it will not move because of the action.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The length of the line in the combinator can be controlled by the distance between two points.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The length of the line in the combinator can be controlled by the distance between two points.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The length of the line in the combinator can be controlled by the distance between two points.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
In addition, you can also use the sewing tool to fix the two points of the costume and the costume room.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
You can also choose the sewing of the line and the line of the costume.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,000
In the costume adjustment, you can start recording the animation.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
You can see that due to the fewer stitches in this animation, the motion between the models is relatively large.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,000
For the skirt with a relatively soft fabric and a larger version, there will be a lot of movement.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
The movements have been changed, but the fabric is still in the position where the last stitch is.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
This will have the feeling that the fabric does not follow the model's body.

19
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
For the skirt with a slightly soft fabric, the movement is not so soft that it may cause the model to bend a little.

20
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
This is mainly because the speed of one stitch is too fast.

21
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Without fully simulation, it can be applied to the next movement.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Play the animation, and you can see that the fabric itself is very soft and close to the body.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Because the action range of the model is no longer close to the body.

24
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
In the case of this, we can see that the movement is the same.

25
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,599
we can change the scene change time and increase the number of action frames

26
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:06,480
Under this number, the costume simulation will be more stable

27
00:02:12,099 --> 00:02:13,900
Then let's take a look at the comparison

28
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:19,520
First, change the scene time to the original 1, so that the number of frames is the same as the original

29
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:24,139
After comparison, you can see that the animation with more frames is more suitable for the real simulation

30
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:27,460
The physical properties of the material will also affect the animation effect

31
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:30,800
The internal damping refers to the rebound coefficient of the material

32
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:37,700
After increasing this value, the material will have resistance, such as in the water, the rebound is slower

33
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:46,660
Observe the model's waist fold, when the internal damping is relatively high, it looks like there is resistance in the environment

34
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,840
In addition, the density will also significantly affect the simulation effect

35
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:57,980
The fabric of the skirt itself is polyester, and the density of the polyester fabric is very low

36
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:05,400
After increasing the density, you can see from the comparison video that when the density becomes larger, the fabric becomes heavier, making it closer to the virtual model

37
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:09,240
And the fold is more obvious, so it looks like it's softer

38
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:16,160
In the usual production process, you can adjust the physical properties and compare them to find a more suitable fabric

